xzram (0.4.1-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * systemd-oomd policy shields session.slice (ManagedOOMPreference=avoid)
    so apps are killed before the compositor and shell
  * Recommended defaults: MGLRU min_ttl_ms=1000, THP defrag=defer+madvise
    (tmpfiles.d), vm.dirty_bytes/dirty_background_bytes, vfs_cache_pressure
  * Doctor: oomd_session_unprotected, thp_always_low_ram

 -- XZram contributors <xzram@example.com>  Wed, 14 Oct 2026 18:00:00 +0100

xzram (0.4.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Recommended defaults enable systemd-oomd with ManagedOOM kill policies
    when no userspace OOM killer is active; rollback undoes it
  * Grow an undersized /swap/swapfile instead of reporting "already matches"
  * Warn when disk swap is on a rotational drive
  * Doctor: OOM kills, memory pressure (PSI), swap headroom, overflow size

 -- XZram contributors <xzram@example.com>  Wed, 14 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0100

xzram (0.3.2-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Security: harden swapfile path handling against symlink races; tighten
    xzramd sandbox and input validation
  * Atomic writes for fstab and all state files; exact fstab entry matching
  * Snapshot restore merges fstab swap entries and removes swapfiles added
    since the snapshot; a failed apply rolls back automatically
  * Swapfile resize keeps the old swap on failure and resizes in place when
    space is tight
  * CLI exit code 3 for unhealthy doctor; non-blocking GUI privileged actions
  * Packaging: Debian source format 3.0 (quilt), watch file, CC0 metadata

 -- XZram contributors <xzram@example.com>  Sun, 11 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0100

xzram (0.3.1-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Fix zram mm_stat field mislabeled as a compression-stream count (now `peak` bytes)
  * Doctor warns (`zram_near_full`) when zram is near full and disk swap absorbs overflow
  * Fix xzramd D-Bus startup registration race (interface now registered before name request)

